Python packages, installed from PyPI
------------------------------------

PyYAML
  MIT License. https://pyyaml.org/
  Required. Parses the show config.

ascmhl (ASC Media Hash List reference implementation)
  MIT License. https://github.com/ascmitc/mhl
  Optional "mhl" extra. Used to read the ASC MHL histories that offload tools
  write beside camera and sound folders. ascmhl in turn depends on, among
  others:
    xxhash (python-xxhash), BSD-2-Clause, https://github.com/ifduyue/python-xxhash
    lxml, BSD-3-Clause, https://lxml.de/
    Click, BSD-3-Clause, https://click.palletsprojects.com/
    pathspec, MPL-2.0, https://github.com/cpburnz/python-pathspec

OpenColorIO (PyPI package "opencolorio")
  BSD-3-Clause. Copyright Contributors to the OpenColorIO Project.
  https://opencolorio.org/
  Optional "colour" extra. Bakes ASC CDL, camera look and show LUT into one
  cube, and produces the independent reference in the colour tests.

pyaaf2
  MIT License. https://github.com/markreidvfx/pyaaf2
  Optional "aaf" extra. Reserved for the AAF stringout stage. The MobID
  layout generated by this software is compatible with it.

pytest and pytest-cov
  MIT License. https://docs.pytest.org/ and https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest-cov
  Optional "dev" extra. Test runner and coverage.

